    "result": "I implemented `shipping_cost` in `solution.py` to follow `spec.md`, and wrote 23 tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 23.\n\nBeyond the spec, I treat NaN and infinite values as `ValueError`. The spec doesn't say what to do with them.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- billable-weight rounding\n- volumetric weight\n- the zone factors\n- free shipping, including the zone 3 exception\n- the oversize surcharge at 120 cm and 121 cm\n- `ROUND_HALF_UP` rounding\n- float handling through `str()`\n- the `TypeError` and `ValueError` cases, including bad zone values like `True` and `1.0`",
